title: `if: false` under the step that runs `node --test`
origin: issue #216 W1. The step held no runner token, so it was no runner site, and the condition that stops the suite passed at warn. v0.6.0 passes it; the same diff on `npx jest` blocks
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 22
      - run: npm ci
      - run: node --test
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 22
      - run: npm ci
      - run: node --test
        if: false
